[Music]  [Music]  do  [Music]  [Music]  hello everyone my name is nari sol and  what you just heard was a new pocket  piece of mind which i'm calling a  nocturn  now when you first think of a nocturn  composers such as frederick chopin and  john field probably come to mind  chopin in particular established the  style of the romantic nocturne as we are  perhaps most familiar with it today  many of his nocturns have a calm and  arpeggiated left hand figure with a  melodic line on top  there's no formal structure to these  character pieces but many of them follow  a ternary form  they are a bit like lullabies that have  been elaborated upon and of course the  main defining characteristic is that a  nocturn is evocative of the night  here are some of my most favorite  nocturns  [Music]  in coming up with my piece i thought of  things that i associate most with the  night  i mostly think of lights and how the  mood of each street corner shifts into  something more mysterious and intense  for me the night is also when i love to  just be in my own space it's when i do  most of my brainstorming work on  projects such as editing these videos or  photos  and decompress with my dog  [Music]  all right  second attempt  this time i have the right cable  so unfortunately i just realized  by the way  thank you mom for this  really nice tote bag  which i use to carry my keyboard  okay  please stand clear  now a question for you all what do you  associate most with the knight and what  is your favorite nocturne  as always thank you so much for watching  and keeping in touch if you'd like to  find more material related to these  videos and my original music please  visit my site  you can also find a link in the  description for my new piano intensive  video course which is an in-depth study  guide into technique harmony and  practice methods while using my modified  chopin exercises thanks again and i'll  see you in the next video  [Music]  you

